        "timestamp": 1777553946,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. DR Congo creates paramilitary mining guard Africa Issued on: 30/04/2026 - 14:59 Democratic Republic of the Congo has announced the creation of a paramilitary force to secure its mining sector, backed by funding from the United States and United Arab Emirates. The unit, expected to grow to over 20,000 personnel by 2028, aims to protect operations, strengthen state control and reassure investors as global competition for critical minerals intensifies. FRANCE 24's Emmet Livingstone has the details from Kinshasa. Mali crisis deepens as separatists and jihadists step up attacks 30/04/2026 Africa Mali faces 'very high risk' of new coup d'état, analyst says, amid jihadist insurgence 29/04/2026 Africa Tuareg rebels urge Russian forces to leave Mali 29/04/2026 Africa 'Over-dependence on military solutions: Mali struggling in its effort to regain peace and security' 29/04/2026 MALI Insurgents reshaping Mali: Tuaregs seek autonomy, jihadists pursue caliphate across Sahel 28/04/2026 MALI Mali capital 'not under threat, but long-term prospects do not look good', analyst says 28/04/2026 Africa Mali's tale of two insurgencies: 'Jihadists seek caliphate while Tuareg rebels pursue autonomy' 27/04/2026 Africa 'Unable to cope': Malian army, Wagner 'overstretched' by Tuareg separatists and jihadist militants 27/04/2026 Africa Russian mercenaries in Mali: Limited gains, reports of abuse 26/04/2026 Africa"
